# A first declaration cannot read its own not-yet-initialized field. A repeated
# receiver writes that same field and may read its previous value on the right:
# `int: x 1; int: x (x + 2)` reads 1 and writes 3. Registration runs ahead of
# emission, so exclude only the physical first declaration during its initializer.
int: l2_own_excl -1
