# K04 S2 part two (ledger section 59; Codex, FABLE-CODEX-20261004-12): why a method that does not read a name
# has it among its hidden inputs.  A row says: method m needs name nm while each of its conditions holds -- m's
# callable formal t holds method a.  A row without conditions: always.  The conditions of row r are the
# l2_dyr_c[r] entries of the pool from l2_dyr_at[r], ordered by formal; a formal stands once in a row.  A row
# is hard when an absent entry would reach a method that reads the name and has no lexical source of its own.
# A call site asks its caller only for the inputs one of whose rows holds for the site's actuals
# (l2_site_needs).  Complete: no number of conditions is fixed.  Compiler metadata: nothing of it exists at run
# time.
